Model answer: B. NADH, C. ATP

ATP and NADH are immediate cellular energy carriers that can rapidly transfer chemical energy to metabolic reactions. ATP donates phosphoryl groups, whereas NADH delivers high-energy electrons to respiration. Glycogen and starch are storage polysaccharides that function as longer-term carbohydrate reserves rather than direct short-term carriers. This distinction is central to metabolic energy flow between storage, catabolism, and ATP-generating pathways.

