Model answer: B. They release energy when they dissipate., C. Energy is required to build them.

Electrochemical gradients store potential energy across membranes. Cells invest energy through electron transport chains or ion pumps to establish these gradients, and energy is released when ions flow down the gradient. They are not encoded in DNA and occur in many organisms, including bacteria, animals, and plants. Such gradients are essential for ATP synthesis and membrane transport processes.

