Model answer: B. 2 Acetyl-CoA, C. 2 NADH

Pyruvate oxidation converts pyruvate into acetyl-CoA before entry into the TCA cycle. Per glucose molecule, two acetyl-CoA and two NADH are produced, together with carbon dioxide. ATP is not generated directly in this step and glucose is the substrate of earlier pathways. The reaction connects glycolysis with mitochondrial aerobic metabolism.

