<<set $totalCorrect += _correctCount>><<set $totalPossible += 2>><<set $incorrectSelections += _wrong>>
Model answer: C. It supplies NADH to the ETC., D. It is also called the Krebs cycle.

The TCA cycle, also known as the Krebs cycle, oxidises acetyl groups and generates reduced cofactors including NADH. These reducing equivalents donate electrons to the electron transport chain for ATP production. The cycle does not occur in the nucleus and does not directly generate glucose. It is a central hub for energy metabolism and biosynthetic precursor formation.

