<<set $totalCorrect += _correctCount>><<set $totalPossible += 1>><<set $incorrectSelections += _wrong>>
Model answer: B. They are released as CO2.

During complete aerobic oxidation, all six carbons originating from glucose are ultimately released as carbon dioxide. Carbon atoms do not become ATP or NADH molecules, and they do not remain permanently within the TCA cycle because cycle intermediates are regenerated. Carbon oxidation coupled to electron transfer underpins energy extraction during respiration.

