<<set $totalCorrect += _correctCount>><<set $totalPossible += 2>><<set $incorrectSelections += _wrong>>
Model answer: A. Ribose-5-phosphate, C. NADPH

The pentose phosphate pathway generates ribose-5-phosphate for nucleotide synthesis and NADPH for reductive biosynthesis and antioxidant defence. ATP and FADH2 are not principal products of this pathway. By supplying reducing power and biosynthetic precursors, the pathway complements glycolysis and supports anabolic metabolism and cellular protection against oxidative damage.

